.TH VUV 7 "October 2026" "vuv 0.9.0" "vuv Manual"
.SH NAME
vuv \- modern C++20 wrapper around libuv
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <vuv/vuv.h>
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vuv
exposes libuv's event loop, handles, and requests through a small,
RAII-friendly C++ API while keeping the underlying
.BR uv_* types
accessible when needed.
.PP
The per-thread singleton
.B vuv::Loop
owns the event loop. Typical lifecycle:
.PP
.RS
Loop::Open() -> init/start/connect/... -> Loop::Run([mode]) -> stop()/close() -> Loop::Close()
.RE
.PP
Key handle families:
.TP
.B Streams
.BR UvStream " (base), " UvTcp ", " UvPipe ", " UvTty
.TP
.B Datagrams
.B UvUdp
.TP
.B Polling
.BR UvPoll ", " UvIdle ", " UvPrepare ", " UvCheck
.TP
.B Timing / deferred
.BR UvTimer ", " Immediate
.TP
.B Cross-thread
.B UvAsync
(uv_async_send; callable from any thread)
.TP
.B Signals
.B UvSignal
.TP
.B Processes
.B UvSpawn
.TP
.B DNS
.BR DNSResolver ", " UvGetAddrInfo
.TP
.B Utilities
.BR UvBufStore ", " HandleSender ", " HandleReceiver
.SH BUILD
.nf
cmake -S . -B build -DVUV_BUILD_TESTS=ON
cmake --build build
ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure
.fi
.SH INSTALL
.nf
cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr/local
cmake --build build
cmake --install build
.fi
.PP
Installed files:
.TP
Library
<prefix>/lib/libvuv.a
.TP
Headers
<prefix>/include/vuv/*.h
.TP
CMake config
<prefix>/lib/cmake/vuv/
.TP
Full manual (Markdown)
<prefix>/share/doc/vuv/vuv-manual.en.md
.TP
This page
<prefix>/share/man/man7/vuv.7
.SH QUICK START
.nf
#include <vuv/vuv.h>

int main() {
    vuv::Loop::Open();
    // ... set up handles ...
    vuv::Loop::Run();
    vuv::Loop::Close();
    return 0;
}
.fi
.PP
Downstream CMake:
.nf
find_package(vuv 0.9 CONFIG REQUIRED)
target_link_libraries(your_target PRIVATE vuv::vuv)
.fi
